    "title": "Jhonkensy Noel homers in 9th to give Columbus Clippers 6-4 win over Buffalo Bisons - NewsBreak",
    "text": "July 23 game: Columbus 6, Buffalo 4 Recap : Jhonkensy Noel hit a two-run homer run in the bottom of the ninth inning to help the Clippers snap a three-game losing streak. The Bisons scored three runs in the top of the ninth to tie the game 4-4. In the bottom of the inning, C.J. Kayfus singled with two outs before Noel homered to end the game. Noel was 3 for 5 with two RBIs, and Petey Halpin added two hits and an RBI. Clippers starter Ryan Webb allowed one run on two hits in 4⅓ innings. He struck out six and walked three. Next game : 12:05 p.m. July 24 vs. Buffalo at Huntington Park Watch : MiLB.TV Radio : 920 AM Ticket info : Call 614-462-5250 or log on to clippersbaseball.com This article originally appeared on The Columbus Dispatch: Jhonkensy Noel homers in 9th to give Columbus Clippers 6-4 win over Buffalo Bisons",
